{
  "_comment": "Synthetic deterministic-categorization golden vector (no real data). One shared set of facts (a catalog = the 23 ported defaults + one user category, a T1 source-category map, a T2 merchant map, and T3 rules) plus a list of cases; each case is one transaction categorized by the first-wins stack CC rules -> T1 -> T2 -> T3, with the expected Decision (category_ref + stage + matched_rule_id) or null for uncategorized. Ground truth for the CC rules, the T3 matcher and normalise_narration was captured from a live run of the web engine's pure helpers (app/services/categorisation/cc_credit_rule.py, cc_debit_rule.py, tier3_rules._matches, app/services/ingestion/normaliser.normalise_narration); the tier ordering/precedence follows the web ingestion pipeline. amount is a string (re-parsed to Decimal - never float); direction Debit|Credit is the statement's own Dr/Cr; category_ref is {builtin: CODE} for one of the 23 defaults or {custom: id} for the user category. Cases: cc-credit-billpay/cc-credit-cashback (a credit-card inflow -> CC rule, cashback preempting the swiggy T2 literal); cc-debit-billpay (bank-side CC payment -> CC rule); t1-source (issuer hint honoured first); t2-literal/t2-regex (merchant memory on the normalised narration); t3-keyword-user/t3-regex-system/t3-amount-range (rules by priority, echoing matched_rule_id); uncategorized (no stage matches).",
  "user_categories": [
    { "id": "user-school-fees", "name": "School Fees", "classification": "SPEND" }
  ],
  "source_map": [
    { "bank_code": "ICICI", "source_category": "Food & Beverage", "category": { "builtin": "FOOD_AND_DINING" } }
  ],
  "merchants": [
